project/witness-importmap-ordering-chromium-blindspot: a puppeteer/Chromium browser-witness can report a spoint page HEALTHY (window.__app.scene populated, 98 meshes) while it is actually BROKEN in Firefox by an importmap-ordering bug. Root cause class: an importmap MUST appear before any <script type=module>/modulepreload, else the browser emits 'Import maps are not allowed after a module load or preload has started' and bare specifiers (e.g. 'three') throw 'bare specifier ... not remapped' in app.js -> client never boots. Chromium tolerated/cache-masked it; Firefox enforces strictly. WITNESS RULE: every live/local witness must explicitly capture console errors matching /import maps are not allowed/i and /bare specifier/i and assert app.js actually executed, NOT just read a possibly-cached window.__app. The fix for the bug itself: in client/index.html keep <script type=importmap> ABOVE the installStyles <script type=module> (installStyles uses a full unpkg URL, no bare specifier, so it can run after the importmap). Fixed 2026-05-31.